[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 746,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 576,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113038,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 576,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Low-grade nasopharyngeal papillary adenocarcinoma is a surface-derived malignant glandular neoplasm showing predominant papillary architecture and indolent behaviour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 747,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 577,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113039,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 577,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8260/3 Low-grade nasopharyngeal papillary adenocarcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 748,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 578,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113040,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 578,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B6B.Y &amp; XH6LV9 Other specified malignant neoplasms of nasopharynx &amp; Papillary adenocarcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 749,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 579,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113041,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 579,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> nasopharyngeal papillary adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> thyroid-like low-grade nasopharyngeal papillary adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 750,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 580,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113042,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113043,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour may occur anywhere in the nasopharynx but most often involves the posterior nasopharyngeal wall {2462370}, the roof of the nasopharynx, and the posterior margin of the nasal septum {33603472}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113044,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common symptoms are nasal obstruction {2462370} and blood-stained rhinorrhoea {33603472}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113045,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour shows no sex predilection and occurs over a wide age range, from the first to the eighth decade of life {2462370; 33603472}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113046,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113047,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>ROS1</em>::<em>GOPC</em> fusion was reported in 1&nbsp;case {33546077}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113048,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Low-grade nasopharyngeal papillary adenocarcinoma is an exophytic, papillary or cauliflower-like lesion with a soft to gritty consistency, measuring from a few millimetres to 40&nbsp;mm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-25T13:49:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113049,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>This is an unencapsulated neoplasm with papillary and glandular growth patterns. The papillae are complex with arborization and fibrovascular cores. Complex (back-to-back) glandular and cribriform/microcystic architectures are present. The cells vary in appearance from pseudostratified columnar to cuboidal. The nuclei are round to oval with vesicular to optically clear chromatin, indistinct nucleoli, and eosinophilic cytoplasm. Mild to moderate nuclear pleomorphism is seen. Scattered mitotic figures can be seen, but atypical mitoses are not present. Squamous differentiation {28601658} and a prominent spindle cell component have been reported {21424532; 32438756}. Psammoma bodies may be present. This tumour has an infiltrative growth into the submucosa. Transition from surface epithelium to carcinoma may be present, supporting a primary nasopharyngeal origin {2462370}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Diffuse immunoreactivity is seen for cytokeratins and EMA. Thyroid transcription factor&nbsp;1 (TTF1) staining is positive (including in spindle and squamous cells) but thyroglobulin and PAX8 are negative {16084450; 28601658; 33546077}. EBV-encoded small RNAs (EBERs), p16, p40/p63, S100, and BRAF p.V600E are negative {21424532; 28601658; 32438756}. Ki-67 staining consistently shows a low proliferation index (&lt;&nbsp;5%).</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The absence of thyroglobulin and PAX8 and the transition from surface epithelium to carcinoma allow for differentiation from papillary thyroid carcinoma. The complexity of papillary and glandular growth, as well as the extensive involvement of the submucosa, would differentiate the tumour from sinonasal papilloma.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-11T16:30:44"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 587,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113050,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 38,
        "headingId": 587,
        "headingText": "<p >Not clinically relevant</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-11T16:30:58"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 758,
